From 2fc66489b82dbb6b5e95e9eb349ded481266d4ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:57:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-121: the CSV table takes typing again -- a real
 double click, and a Chinese input method (0.121.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20261001: "表格我沒辦法寫入" (screenshot: Mot_Table.csv in the table, a cell selected, nothing
could be written). Reproduced with REAL input (DevTools protocol), which the synthetic-event test
had missed:
- a real double click opened nothing: the first press redraws the grid, so the second click's
  target is a new element and Chromium aims the dblclick at the common ancestor (#grid). Now the
  second press's click count (e.detail >= 2) opens the editor, its text selected.
- with an IME on (注音 / 倉頡) typing did nothing: the keys went to the grid div, which takes no IME.
  Now ONE input (#kb) always holds the keys: idle it sits, invisible, on the current cell; a typed
  character or an IME word starting goes into it and makes it that cell's editor (Excel: typing
  replaces the cell). The IME's own Enter (isComposing / 229) picks the word, it does not write.
  A click on the table's empty part / VS Code focusing the editor hands the focus back to it.

Tests: new test/csv_realinput.js (headless Edge + CDP Input.*: real double click, real keys, an IME
composition "ㄨ" -> "中", a click on the empty part) -- 4/4 on this version, 4/4 FAIL on 0.120.0;
csv_driver.js adds a double click (detail 2) and an IME composition. run_all: 3/3 layers pass
(lib 166, smoke 194). The real VS Code layer not run: VS Code's own update (since 05:41) still
holds its lock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
